# Build-context ignore rules specific to deploy/mineru.Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit looks for `<Dockerfile path>.dockerignore` first, falling back to the
# `.dockerignore` at the build context root only if that's not found. Since compose sets the
# context to the repo root (..), and this Dockerfile doesn't actually COPY any file, we ignore
# everything outright here --
# otherwise docker would package up template_files/ (hundreds of MB of copyrighted PDFs) and
# data/ and ship them to the daemon for nothing, wasting several minutes.
#
# If a repo file ever genuinely needs to be COPYed into the image, add a negation rule here,
# e.g.:
#   !runners/mineru_runner.py
*
